{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":121916,"duration_api_ms":235706,"num_turns":9,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"65ce979b-54af-45b6-9b04-657b42b42c0b","total_cost_usd":0.6794022999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":3961,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35222,"cache_read_input_tokens":86407,"output_tokens":5200,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5179,"outputTokens":11588,"cacheReadInputTokens":742423,"cacheCreationInputTokens":103116,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.2662563,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3961,"outputTokens":5200,"cacheReadInputTokens":86407,"cacheCreationInputTokens":35222,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.413146,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Rejected four amendments where code inspection showed the claimed bugs are already fixed or based on incorrect premises. Accepted three amendments identifying real defects: shrimp feeding/condition inconsistency, AddShrimp bypassing cohort seeding, and missing snapshot backward compatibility for shrimp-stage fields.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bbde1d06","decision":"reject","rationale":"The bug described is already fixed. save.rs has a v8→v9 migration (`normalize_legacy_algae_half_saturation_fields_in_save()`) that removes the old `algae_half_saturation_*_mg_total` keys, divides by LEGACY_KINETIC_REFERENCE_VOLUME_L (20.0), and inserts the rescaled values under the new field names. This function is also called unconditionally before serde deserialization (save.rs ~line 207-208), so old saves are correctly rescaled before the serde aliases could ever map stale values. The planner's rationale that 'save.rs has no migration that renames or rescales those algae fields' is factually incorrect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-b5ce6a89","decision":"reject","rationale":"Already implemented. migrate_v7_to_v8 in save.rs (lines 682-729) renames plant_half_saturation_*_mg_total fields to the new names and rescales them using legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l() (÷20) and legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_m2() (÷0.1). A comprehensive test in save_load.rs uses non-default legacy values (13.0, 2.8, 34.0) and verifies all five converted fields with 1e-12 tolerance. The claimed silent reset does not occur."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-bc482e98","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's premise is wrong. SubstrateLayerState::default() sets colonizable_area_factor to 0.0, not 0.5. resolved_colonizable_area_factor() checks if the factor is finite AND > 0.0; since 0.0 fails that check, it falls back to kind.default_colonizable_area_factor(). For CoarsePorous that returns 0.9. So a CoarsePorous layer built with ..Default::default() correctly resolves to 0.9, matching the test's expectation. The test is not broken."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-f57688d0","decision":"reject","rationale":"The normalization function already handles algae fields. normalize_legacy_process_params_preset() (presets.rs lines 1242-1262) explicitly removes algae_half_saturation_n_mg_total and algae_half_saturation_p_mg_total, converts them via legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l(), and inserts the rescaled values under the new names. The amendment's claim that the function 'no longer handles the old algae field names' is incorrect — the code does handle them."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-4901e64f","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed real inconsistency. shrimp_feeding() (line 141) computes food_demand_biomass_g = total_feeding_units * rate * grazing_access_factor, but update_condition() (lines 267-273) computes target_food_g = total_feeding_units * rate without grazing_access_factor. Since grazing_access_factor defaults to < 1.0, shrimp that consume their full accessible ration are measured against an inflated target, producing systematic condition/reproduction/maturation penalties in all tanks with non-trivial substrate."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-17d200a6","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed real bug. PlayerAction::AddShrimp (engine.rs:691-693) does adult.count.saturating_add(count) with no other state updates. StageCohort::receive_entrants() (biology.rs:97-123) handles both empty-cohort seeding (resets condition_index, reserve_g, maturation_accum) and non-empty merging (weighted condition averaging). By bypassing this, purchased shrimp inherit stale condition_index from a dead or degraded cohort instead of arriving healthy, and reserve_g is never initialized for the newcomers."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-dce4c34e","decision":"accept","rationale":"Confirmed real compatibility gap. TankSnapshotRepr requires total_shrimp_count and sub_adult_count with no #[serde(default)] attributes. normalize_snapshot_object() only iterates LEGACY_SNAPSHOT_CHEMISTRY_FIELD_ALIASES — zero handling for shrimp-stage fields. tank_tui deserializes via serde_json::from_value through this path. A pre-stage server payload lacking the new fields will fail deserialization rather than defaulting sub_adult_count to 0 and computing the total."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"6991e68e-93c3-4300-aab8-104b30c7bded"}
